name>Watt</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Walker</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Maher</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>BG</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>The growing burden of tuberculosis: global trends and interactions with the HIV epidemic.</article-title><source>Arch Intern Med</source><volume>163</volume><fpage>1009</fpage><lpage>1021</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12742798</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000735-Flynn1"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Flynn</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Chan</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Immunology of tuberculosis.</article-title><source>Annu Rev Immunol</source><volume>19</volume><fpage>93</fpage><lpage>129</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11244032</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000735-Kaufmann1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kaufmann</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>How can immunology contribute to the control of tuberculosis?</article-title><source>Nat Rev Immunol</source><volume>1</volume><fpage>20</fpage><lpage>30</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11905811</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000735-Tesfa1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tesfa</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Koch</surname><given-names>FW</given-names></name><name><surname>Pankow</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Volk</surname><given-names>HD</given-names></name><name><surname>Kern</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Confirmation of Mycobacterium tuberculosis infection by flow cytometry after ex vivo incubation of peripheral blood T cells with an ESAT-6-derived peptide pool.</article-title><source>Cytometry</source><volume>60B</volume><fpage>47</fpage><lpage>53</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15221869</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000735-Hamann1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hamann</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Baars</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Rep</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>Hooibrink</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Kerkhof-Garde</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Phenotypic and functional separation of memory and effector human CD8&#x0002b; T cells.</article-title><source>J Exp Med</source><volume>186</volume><fpage>1407</fpage><lpage>1418</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9348298</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000735-Sallusto1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sallusto</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Lenig</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Forster</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Lipp</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Lanzavecchia</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Two subsets of memory T lymphocytes with distinct homing potentials and effector functions.</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>401</volume><fpage>708</fpage><lpage>712</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10537110</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000735-Wills1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wills</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Okecha</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Weekes</surname><given-names>MP</given-names></name><name><surname>Gandhi</surname><given-names>MK</given-names></name><name><surname>Sissons</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Identification of naive or antigen-experienced human CD8(&#x0002b;) T cells by expression of costimulation and chemokine receptors: analysis of the human cytomegalovirus-specific CD8(&#x0002b;) T cell response.</article-title><source>J Immunol</source><volume>168</volume><fpage>5455</fpage><lpage>5464</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12023339</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000735-Appay1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Appay</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Zaunders</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Papagno</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Sutton</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Jaramillo</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Characterization of CD4(&#x0002b;) CTLs ex vivo.</article-title><source>J Immunol</source><volume>168</volume><fpage>5954</fpage><lpage>5958</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12023402</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000735-Kern1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kern</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>LiPira</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Gratama</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Manca</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Roederer</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Measuring Ag-specific immune responses: understanding